         <sch:assert test="(self::Class and //ExternalRefBaseObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Class ',concat(' ',@typeRef,' '))]) or (self::ExternalOwlClass and //ExternalRefBaseObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' ExternalOwlClass ',concat(' ',@typeRef,' '))]) or (self::Class and //SubObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Class ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))]) or (self::ExternalOwlClass and //SubObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' ExternalOwlClass ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))]) or (self::Class and //Class[@uid = $uidRef]) or (self::ClassString) or (self::ExternalOwlClass and //ExternalOwlClass[@uid = $uidRef])">(ActivityMethodAssignment : <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) The ActivityMethodAssignment.Role contains a bad reference (<sch:value-of select="$uidRef"/>) must be an element of ClassSelect.</sch:assert>
