rLinePoint  LeaderLinePointWithSurface  DegeneratePcurve  PointOnCurve  PointOnSurface ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Surface  OrientedSurface  Plane  RectangularTrimmedSurface ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' AdvancedFace ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' ConnectedFaceSet ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' EdgeCurve  EdgeBoundedCurveWithLength ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' EdgeLoop ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' VertexPoint ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' TopologicalRepresentationItem  ConnectedEdgeSet  ConnectedEdgeSubSet  Edge  EdgeCurve  EdgeBoundedCurveWithLength  SubEdge  FaceSurface  Path  Vertex  VertexPoint ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))]">(GeometricIntersection : <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) The GeometricIntersection.RepresentedGeometry contains a bad reference (<sch:value-of select="$uidRef"/>) must be an element of ShapeElementRepresentedGeometrySelect.</sch:assert>
      </sch:rule>
   </sch:pattern>
   <!--- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -->
   <!--GeometricModel set of rules-->
   <!--(Inverse of GeometricCoordinateSpace.Representations :: PartProperty) GeometricRepresentation.ContextOfItems : GeometricCoordinateSpace => no rule needed when PartProperty or Optional-->
   <!--(Rule specific to Id construct) Representation.Id : IdentifierSelect-->
   <sch:pattern id="GeometricModel_Id">
      <sch:rule context="//*[@uid and ((self::SubObject and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel') or (self::Representation and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel'))]/Id">
         <sch:let name="uid" value="../@uid"/>
         <sch:let name="directId" value="@id"/>
         <sch:assert test="(count($directId) != 0 or count(Identifier/@id) != 0) and (count($directId) != 1 or count(Identifier/@id) = 0)">(GeometricModel : <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) The GeometricModel.Id shall be defined with exactly one of the following construct Id/@id or Identifier/@id.</sch:assert>
      </sch:rule>
   </sch:pattern>
   <!--(Rule specific to Id construct) Representation.VersionId : OPTIONAL IdentifierSelect-->
   <sch:pattern id="GeometricModel_VersionId">
      <sch:rule context="//*[@uid and ((self::SubObject and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel') or (self::Representation and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel'))]/VersionId">
         <sch:let name="uid" value="../@uid"/>
         <sch:let name="directId" value="@id"/>
         <sch:assert test="(count($directId) != 0 or count(Identifier/@id) != 0) and (count($directId) != 1 or count(Identifier/@id) = 0)">(GeometricModel : <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) The GeometricModel.VersionId shall be defined with exactly one of the following construct Id/@id or Identifier/@id.</sch:assert>
      </sch:rule>
   </sch:pattern>
   <!--(Reference to Entity) Representation.ClassifiedAs : OPTIONAL SET[1:unbounded] OF Classification (kind=AGGREGATE - cardinality=OPTIONAL SET[1:unbounded] OF  - redefined=false)-->
   <sch:pattern id="GeometricModel_ClassifiedAs">
      <sch:rule context="//*[@uid and ((self::SubObject and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel') or (self::Representation and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel'))]/ClassifiedAs/Classification">
         <sch:let name="uid" value="../../@uid"/>
         <sch:let name="uidRef" value="@uidRef"/>
         <sch:assert test="//ExternalRefBaseObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Classification ',concat(' ',@typeRef,' '))] or //SubObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Classification ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //Classification[@uid = $uidRef]">(GeometricModel : <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) The GeometricModel.ClassifiedAs contains a bad reference (<sch:value-of select="$uidRef"/>) must be of type Classification.</sch:assert>
      </sch:rule>
   </sch:pattern>
   <!--(Reference to Entity) Representation.Items : SET[1:unbounded] OF RepresentationItem (kind=AGGREGATE - cardinality=SET[1:unbounded] OF  - redefined=false)-->
   <sch:pattern id="GeometricModel_Items">
      <sch:rule context="//*[@uid and ((self::SubObject and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel') or (self::Representation and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel'))]/Items/RepresentationItem">
         <sch:let name="uid" value="../../@uid"/>
         <sch:let name="uidRef" value="@uidRef"/>
         <sch:assert test="//ExternalRefBaseObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' RepresentationItem  Callout  DetailedGeometricModelItem  AdvancedFace  AxisPlacement  ToolAttachmentPointFrame  ToolCentrePointFrame  CameraModel3D  Cartesian11  ClippingOperator  ConnectedFaceSet  Curve  BoundedCurve  BoundedCurveWithLength  CompositeCurveOnSurface  Pcurve  SurfaceCurve  TrimmedCurve  Curve11  Cylindrical11  Direction  EdgeLoop  GeometricPlaceholderSet  GeometricSet  GeometricCurveSet  BoundaryCurveSet  InterpolatedConfigurationSequence  KinematicPair  HighOrderKinematicPair  LowOrderKinematicPair  LowOrderKinematicPairWithMotionCoupling  KinematicPairValue  KinematicPairWithMotionCoupling  KinematicPathDefinedByNodes  LightSource  Loop  PlanarBox  Point  CartesianPoint  LeaderLinePoint  LeaderLinePointWithSurface  DegeneratePcurve  PointOnCurve  PointOnSurface  PointAndVector  PointArray  Polar11  RotationAboutDirection  Surface  OrientedSurface  Plane  RectangularTrimmedSurface  TessellatedItem  ExternalRepresentationItem  ExternalTessellatedAnnotation  StyledElement  AnnotationElement  AnnotationPlaceholderOccurrence  AnnotationPlane  TessellatedAnnotation  OverRidingStyledElement  ContextDependentOverRidingStyledElement  StyledModelReplication  TopologicalRepresentationItem  ConnectedEdgeSet  ConnectedEdgeSubSet  Edge  EdgeCurve  EdgeBoundedCurveWithLength  SubEdge  FaceSurface  Path  Vertex  VertexPoint  UserDefined11 ',concat(' ',@typeRef,' '))] or //SubObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' RepresentationItem  Callout  DetailedGeometricModelItem  AdvancedFace  AxisPlacement  ToolAttachmentPointFrame  ToolCentrePointFrame  CameraModel3D  Cartesian11  ClippingOperator  ConnectedFaceSet  Curve  BoundedCurve  BoundedCurveWithLength  CompositeCurveOnSurface  Pcurve  SurfaceCurve  TrimmedCurve  Curve11  Cylindrical11  Direction  EdgeLoop  GeometricPlaceholderSet  GeometricSet  GeometricCurveSet  BoundaryCurveSet  InterpolatedConfigurationSequence  KinematicPair  HighOrderKinematicPair  LowOrderKinematicPair  LowOrderKinematicPairWithMotionCoupling  KinematicPairValue  KinematicPairWithMotionCoupling  KinematicPathDefinedByNodes  LightSource  Loop  PlanarBox  Point  CartesianPoint  LeaderLinePoint  LeaderLinePointWithSurface  DegeneratePcurve  PointOnCurve  PointOnSurface  PointAndVector  PointArray  Polar11  RotationAboutDirection  Surface  OrientedSurface  Plane  RectangularTrimmedSurface  TessellatedItem  ExternalRepresentationItem  ExternalTessellatedAnnotation  StyledElement  AnnotationElement  AnnotationPlaceholderOccurrence  AnnotationPlane  TessellatedAnnotation  OverRidingStyledElement  ContextDependentOverRidingStyledElement  StyledModelReplication  TopologicalRepresentationItem  ConnectedEdgeSet  ConnectedEdgeSubSet  Edge  EdgeCurve  EdgeBoundedCurveWithLength  SubEdge  FaceSurface  Path  Vertex  VertexPoint  UserDefined11 ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef]">(GeometricModel : <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) The GeometricModel.Items contains a bad reference (<sch:value-of select="$uidRef"/>) must be of type RepresentationItem.</sch:assert>
      </sch:rule>
   </sch:pattern>
   <!--(Reference to Select) Representation.RepresentationTypes : OPTIONAL SET[1:unbounded] OF ClassSelect (kind=AGGREGATE - cardinality=OPTIONAL SET[1:unbounded] OF  - redefined=false)-->
   <sch:pattern id="GeometricModel_RepresentationTypes">
      <sch:rule context="//*[@uid and ((self::SubObject and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel') or (self::Representation and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricModel'))]/RepresentationTypes/*">
         <sch:let name="uid" value="../../@uid"/>
         <sch:let name="uidRef" value="@uidRef"/>
         <sch:assert test="(self::Class and //ExternalRefBaseObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Class ',concat(' ',@typeRef,' '))]) or (self::ExternalOwlClass and //ExternalRefBaseObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' ExternalOwlClass ',concat(' ',@typeRef,' '))]) or (self::Class and //SubObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Class ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))]) or (self::ExternalOwlClass and //SubObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' ExternalOwlClass ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))]) or (self::Class and //Class[@uid = $uidRef]) or (self::ClassString) or (self::ExternalOwlClass and //ExternalOwlClass[@uid = $uidRef])">(GeometricModel : <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) The GeometricModel.RepresentationTypes contains a bad reference (<sch:value-of select="$uidRef"/>) must be an element of ClassSelect.</sch:assert>
      </sch:rule>
   </sch:pattern>
   <!--(Inverse of RepresentationContext.Representations :: PartProperty) Representation.ContextOfItems : RepresentationContext => no rule needed when PartProperty or Optional-->
   <!--- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -->
   <!--GeometricPlaceholderSet set of rules-->
   <!--(Reference to Select) GeometricPlaceholderSet.Elements : SET[1:unbounded] OF GeometricPlaceholderSetSelect (kind=AGGREGATE - cardinality=SET[1:unbounded] OF  - redefined=false)-->
   <sch:pattern id="GeometricPlaceholderSet_Elements">
      <sch:rule context="//*[@uid and ((self::SubObject and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricPlaceholderSet') or (self::RepresentationItem and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='GeometricPlaceholderSet'))]/Elements/*">
         <sch:let name="uid" value="../../@uid"/>
