         <sch:assert test="//ExternalRefBaseObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Edge  EdgeCurve  EdgeBoundedCurveWithLength  SubEdge ',concat(' ',@typeRef,' '))] or //SubObject[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Edge  EdgeCurve  EdgeBoundedCurveWithLength  SubEdge ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))] or //RepresentationItem[@uid = $uidRef and contains(' Edge  EdgeCurve  EdgeBoundedCurveWithLength  SubEdge ',concat(' ',substring-after(@xsi:type,':'),' '))]">(Path : <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) The Path.EdgeList contains a bad reference (<sch:value-of select="$uidRef"/>) must be of type Edge.</sch:assert>
      </sch:rule>
   </sch:pattern>
   <!--(Rule Path.WR1)-->
   <sch:pattern id="Path_WR1"><sch:rule context="//RepresentationItem[@uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='Path']"> <sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/> <sch:let name="edgeList" value="child::EdgeList/Edge/@uidRef"/> <sch:assert test="every $j in for $i in $edgeList return ( (if ((child::OrientationList/Boolean[index-of($edgeList, $i)]) eq 'true' ) then //*[@uid=$i]/EdgeEnd/@uidRef else //*[@uid=$i]/EdgeStart/@uidRef) eq (if (child::OrientationList/Boolean[1+index-of($edgeList, $i) ] eq 'true') then //*[@uid=$edgeList[1+index-of($edgeList, $i)]]/EdgeStart/@uidRef else //*[@uid=$edgeList[1+index-of($edgeList, $i)]]/EdgeEnd/@uidRef )) satisfies $j=true()">(Path.WR1 <sch:value-of select="$uid"/>) the end Vertex of each Edge (<sch:value-of select="$edgeList"/>) shall be the same as the start Vertex of its successor.</sch:assert> </sch:rule></sch:pattern>
   <!--- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -->
